{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "1CH",
  "chapter": 18,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1CH.18.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.18.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now after this it came to pass that David smote the Philistines, and subdued them, and took Gath and its towns out of the hand of the Philistines.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.18.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.18.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he smote Moab; and the Moabites became David's servants, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " brought gifts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.18.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.18.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David smote Hadarezer king of Zobah to Hamath, as he went to establish his dominion by the river Euphrates.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.18.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.18.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David took from him a thousand chariots, and seven thousand horsemen, and twenty thousand footmen: David also houghed all the chariot -",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": " horses",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", but reserved of them a hundred chariots.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.18.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.18.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when the Syrians of Damascus came to help Hadarezer king of Zobah, David slew of the Syrians two and twenty thousand men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.18.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.18.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then David put ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "garrisons",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in Syria-damascus; and the Syrians became David's servants, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " brought gifts. Thus the LORD preserved David whithersoever he went.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.18.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.18.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David took the shields of gold that were on the servants of Hadarezer, and brought them to Jerusalem.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.18.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.18.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Likewise from Tibhath, and from Chun, cities of Hadarezer, David brought very much brass, with which Solomon made the brazen sea, and the pillars, and the vessels of brass.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.18.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.18.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now when Tou king of Hamath heard how David had smitten all the host of Hadarezer king of Zobah;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.18.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.18.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He sent Hadoram his son to king David to inquire of his welfare, and to congratulate him, because he had fought against Hadarezer, and smitten him; (for Hadarezer had warred with Tou;) and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all manner of vessels of gold, and silver, and brass.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.18.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.18.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Them also king David dedicated to the LORD, with the silver and the gold that he brought from all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "these",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " nations; from Edom, and from Moab, and from the children of Ammon, and from the Philistines, and from Amalek.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.18.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.18.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Moreover, Abishai the son of Zeruiah slew of the Edomites in the valley of salt eighteen thousand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.18.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.18.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he put garrisons in Edom; and all the Edomites became David's servants. Thus the LORD preserved David whithersoever he went.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.18.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.18.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So David reigned over all Israel, and executed judgment and justice among all his people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.18.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.18.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Joab the son of Zeruiah ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " over the host; and Jehoshaphat the son of Ahilud, recorder;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.18.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.18.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Zadok the son of Ahitub, and Abimelech the son of Abiathar, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the priests; and Shavsha was scribe;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.18.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.18.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " over the Cherethites and the Pelethites; and the sons of David ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " chief about the king.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
